CADMUS-CR-16 · Secure Coding Mobile · session folder
=====================================================

This folder ($CR_SESSION_DIR/$CR_SESSION = {{ cr16_home }}/cr-session/cr16) is
where the course validators look for the files you produce. Run them with:

    python3 /opt/cadmus/cr1_validate.py --level A1 --session $CR_SESSION
    python3 /opt/cadmus/cr2_validate.py --session $CR_SESSION --checkpoint all
    python3 /opt/cadmus/cr3_validate.py --session $CR_SESSION --level D1
    python3 /opt/cadmus/cr4_validate.py --session $CR_SESSION --level E2

File                     Level   Content
-----------------------  ------  ---------------------------------------------------
a1_artefact.json         CR1 A1  {"apk_sha256": "<sha256sum app-release.apk>",
                                  "version_name": "1.2.0", "version_code": 3}
mobsf_report.json        CR1 A2  MobSF JSON report:
                                  curl -X POST -d "hash=$H" -H "Authorization: $MOBSF_KEY" \
                                       $MOBSF/api/v1/report_json -o mobsf_report.json
zap_alerts.json          CR1 A2  curl -s $ZAP/JSON/core/view/alerts/ -o zap_alerts.json
  (or zap_alerts.xml)            curl -s $ZAP/OTHER/core/other/xmlreport/ -o zap_alerts.xml
a3_counts.json           CR1 A3  {"vulnerabilities": 0, "bugs": 0, "code_smells": 0,
                                  "security_hotspots": 0, "quality_profile": "Sonar way"}
                                 (your numbers from the SonarQube dashboard)
findings.md              CR1 A4  your findings report (cr1_validate.py --level A4
                                  --session $CR_SESSION --report findings.md)
cr1_findings.json        CR4 E2  {"findings": [{"id": "VB-CR1-01"}, ...]} - the IDs of
                                  your CR1 report, so authored scenarios can cite them
dependency_register.json CR3 D1  the triaged register (CR3_Dependency_Register_Template.md)
vex.json                 CR3 D3  durable records for carried-forward advisories
risk_exposure.md         CR3 D3  residual exposure statement (more than 200 characters)
pipeline_run.json        CR4 E3  record of the complete pipeline run
evidence_bundle.json     CR4 E3  release digest, SBOM, scenario results
residual_coverage.md     CR4 E3  what the pipeline cannot detect

Read by the validators from the project instead:
  ~/vulnbank/app/build/reports/dependency-check-report.json   ./gradlew dependencyCheckAnalyze
  ~/vulnbank/build/reports/bom.json                           ./gradlew cyclonedxBom
  ~/vulnbank/gradle/verification-metadata.xml                 ./gradlew --write-verification-metadata sha256,pgp help
  ~/vulnbank/.github/workflows/security.yml                   CR4 E1
  ~/vulnbank/exploits/run_scenarios.py                        CR4 E2: cp -r /opt/cadmus/exploits ~/vulnbank/

SonarQube (CR1 A3): export SONAR_TOKEN=<a *user* token of your SonarQube account>;
the A3 validator reads the project with it (SONAR_ADMIN_TOKEN, if set, wins).
